+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Merge Patch and returns the
+merged document as a new value; neither argument is mutated. The algorithm is the one of RFC 7386 section 2
+(restated unchanged by RFC 7396, which obsoletes it). A patch that is not an object replaces the target
+whole; an object patch is merged member by member, a `null` member removing the target's member, and a
+target that is not an object being treated as `{}`. Arrays are replaced, not merged, so a merge patch cannot
+set a member to `null`. It never throws. Only own members are read, and `__proto__` is handled as plain data.
